    "body": "## Summary\nThe MooncakeStoreConnector guide did not mention `kv_load_failure_policy`. With the default `\"fail\"`, a failed KV load returns an empty response, which surprises anyone running a store-backed deployment.\n\n## Changes\n- Describe `kv_load_failure_policy`: accepted values, the default, and what each one does.\n- Add a config example that uses `\"recompute\"` for store-backed setups.\n\n## Testing\n- Docs build and pre-commit markdown checks\n\nCloses #62866\n\n## Demo\n\n![demo](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mvanhorn/pr-demo-assets/main/vllm/mooncake-load-failure-policy-docs/demo.gif)\n\n<video src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mvanhorn/pr-demo-assets/main/vllm/mooncake-load-failure-policy-docs/demo.mp4\" controls width=\"720\"></video>\n",
